# Deliberately untracked segments.
#
# These are real corpus members. They exist on disk, they are indexed, outlines
# and renderers reference them normally, and the checker verifies them. They are
# simply not committed.
#
# The distinction is publication, not validity — so do not "clean this up" on the
# grounds that a listed file is missing from git, and do not delete a file because
# it is listed here. If you are auditing completeness, the corpus on disk is the
# corpus; git holds a subset by design (see README, "What is on disk but not in git").
#
# Bare filenames match at any depth, so an entry survives a segment moving from
# .to-integrate/ into its type directory.

# Religious imagery and scripture. Joseph's own standing constraint, stated in the
# same message the segment quotes: "You are welcome to record religious imagery and
# scripture in the claude memories here. We'll probably refrain from doing so in the
# public repo here other than obliquely." Said of archema-io; ruled to apply here
# 2026-07-30. The segment carries the constraint in its own body as well, so the
# reason travels with it if this file is ever lost.
exm-i-was-once-like-you.udon
